items.change:
Extend LyricsModel::Line to {startMs, endMs, text, words[{startMs, endMs, text, syllable flag}], background (text + words), agent}, and stop deleting word stamps. Write our own parsers and store the raw payload plus a format tag, so later parser fixes also apply to stored lyrics:
- enhanced LRC;
- karaoke LRC in both QQ/NetEase readings, keeping the one that attaches more text;
- Apple TTML through QtCore's QXmlStreamReader (no new Qt module), reading ttm:agent namespace-aware and accepting clocks like '27.395', '1:05.20', '1:02:03.4', '1.5s' and '250ms';
- LyricsPlus syllable JSON;
- a format sniffer that tries TTML, then karaoke, then enhanced LRC, then LRC, then plain.

Keep inactive lines as today's single Text. For the current line, when it has word timing, load a WordLine component:
- a Flow of per-word Text items (per syllable for CJK) that turn from neutral600 to ink as they are sung;
- a left-to-right wipe inside the active word, driven by a FrameAnimation that interpolates the player clock between position updates, treating a jump over 1.25 s as a seek;
- mirrored for RTL lines, and whole words for joined scripts such as Arabic.
Words get their own small lead (0-50 ms, tuned by ear) instead of the line's 150 ms, and there is no scaling or glow, per DESIGN.md.
